    "narrative": "The Austin Waves roster presents a balanced, albeit challenging, slate for May 11th. **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier play (64.87) against Ryan Weathers; despite the platoon disadvantage, his elite speed profiles well against the slow delivery of Weathers, and his primary spot at the top of the lineup maximizes his plate appearances. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** (63.06) is an aggressive start, benefiting significantly from the soft 5.30 xERA of Roki Sasaki, which provides a high ceiling despite the daunting reputation of the arm. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.38) and **Coby Mayo** (56.63) both hover near the strong threshold, they are buoyed by stable order positioning, though they remain sensitive to the outcome of pending lineup confirmations.\n\nThe bench decision for **Josh Jung** (48.40) was the most difficult, as he ultimately missed the cut behind **Nolan Schanuel** and **Josh Lowe**. While **Josh Jung** offers respectable pop against Michael Soroka, the optimizer favored the higher overall volume and situational alignment of the starting eight. We are exercising caution with **Kyle Tucker** (53.52) and **Andy Pages** (47.06) today; both face Trevor McDonald, whose 2.60 xERA suppresses their respective scoring ceilings significantly. Specifically, **Andy Pages** faces the additional hurdle of an elite defensive catcher, which lowers his efficiency score further. We will monitor the weather and final lineups closely, as the scarcity of stolen bases means that if **Gunnar Henderson** or **Josh Lowe** are dropped in the batting order, we may need to pivot to preserve our game caps.",
